          <section class="recipe-section" id="spec-fields">
            <h3 class="recipe-section__heading">What a spec can say</h3>
            <p class="recipe-section__body">Everything else has a default:</p>
            <table class="recipe-table">
              <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Default</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>version</code></td><td>1</td><td>The only version there is</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>branch</code></td><td><code>convoy/&lt;name&gt;-&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Where the work lands. Never the branch you have checked out</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>concurrency</code></td><td>4</td><td>Tasks at once; <code>--concurrency</code> overrides it</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>on_failure</code></td><td><code>continue</code></td><td><code>continue</code> skips only what depends on a failed task; <code>stop</code> starts nothing new</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>adapter</code></td><td>the one <code>opencastle init</code> set up</td><td>The runtime, for this spec</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>gates</code>, <code>gate_retries</code></td><td>none, 0</td><td>Commands run once at the end, and how many fix attempts a failure gets</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>defaults.timeout</code>, <code>timeout</code></td><td><code>30m</code></td><td>Per task</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>defaults.max_retries</code>, <code>max_retries</code></td><td>1</td><td>Attempts after the first</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>defaults.review</code>, <code>review</code></td><td><code>auto</code></td><td><code>auto</code> passes a writer's change, and one of at most 10 lines in 2 files, without a reviewer — never one in <code>auth/</code>, <code>security/</code>, <code>migrations/</code> or <code>rls/</code>, or from the security or data agent; <code>fast</code> always reviews; <code>panel</code> asks three reviewers; <code>none</code> skips</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>defaults.model</code>, <code>model</code></td><td>by the agent's tier</td><td>The model, for every task or for one</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>defaults.permission_mode</code></td><td><code>acceptEdits</code></td><td>What the agents may do: <code>default</code>, <code>acceptEdits</code>, <code>auto</code>, <code>dontAsk</code>, <code>bypassPermissions</code> or <code>plan</code></td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
            <p class="recipe-section__body">
              The planner writes the same format; open any spec in <code>.opencastle/convoys/</code> for another
              example. How the engine reads it is in
              <a href="https://github.com/monkilabs/opencastle/blob/main/ARCHITECTURE.md#spec-defaults">ARCHITECTURE.md</a>.
            </p>
